/-!
# (key: heads-first) The BODY network of a cross-replica network and a set of head bins

Given p-a3's network `N : XNetW` and a set `hb` of A4 host bins `(ρ, j)` (the heads: never hosted, remaining climb
48), with a block `blockMat (z l)` per head role `l` such that `blockMat (z l) * X0` reaches the A4 end frame `X1` for
free (`hz`; the geometry gives `X1 = shift c * blockMat z * X0`), `XNetW.toHF` is the network `N'` (an `XNetHW`) in which
* the head bins' A4 chain is constantly `blockMat z * X0` (the head block already applied: `hd = blockMat z`),
* their remaining climb is `0` (`hrem' = 0`), the free shift being the end step;
* everything else is `N`'s.
`XNetW.unit_toHF`: `N'.unit = N.unit - |hb| * φ 48` (when `N.hrem = 48` on `hb`).
Written by p-hfirst (wht45/lever, 19 Oct 2026); the field list of `XNetW.toHF` is generated by
p-hfirst/tools/mk_xneth.py from p-a3's TDef.lean; prepared with assistance from Claude.  No `sorry`.
WARP variant (ToHF): generated by x-inst/tools/mk_hfw2979.py (wht45/lever2979, 19 Oct 2026) from
p-hfirst's file of the same name (sha256 pinned in tools/hfw2979-inputs.sha256), with p-a3's mk_warp.py
substitutions (providers `GInvW .. Ok`, window facts `hok0 .. hok8`, stages `gistageW_fwd/bwd`).
-/

